# The build context for three of the Go images is backend/, because they resolve commons-go
# through `replace ../commons-go` and need it inside the context. That pulls in all six
# components, so build output and local noise are excluded explicitly.
*/dist/
*/*/dist/
**/.git
**/*.exe
**/node_modules/

# api-linter-service's builder downloads its own linters into resources/. A copy downloaded
# on the host must not reach the context in their place. These rules lived in
# api-linter-service/.dockerignore, which a backend/ context never reads, so until now they
# did not apply to the image at all.
api-linter-service/resources/spectral/linux/spectral
api-linter-service/resources/spectral/windows/spectral.exe
api-linter-service/resources/vacuum/linux/vacuum
api-linter-service/resources/vacuum/windows/vacuum.exe
